Script.script:
-- ============================================================
-- DslColors v1.0 RELEASE
-- Dark and Shattered Lands / Mudlet identity-color helper
-- ============================================================
--
-- WHAT THIS PACKAGE DOES
--   DslColors watches visible Mudlet console lines and adds color to stable
--   identity terms without rewriting the game text. It is designed for DSL's
--   WHO-style output and related lists, where race, class, kingdom, clan, robe,
--   dragon type, titles, and learned player names can all appear in one line.
--
-- CORE GOALS
--   1. Color DSL race/class/org/title terms consistently.
--   2. Learn people conservatively from WHO / WHOK / WHOC / WHOCRAFT output.
--   3. Preserve richer WHO data when shorter kingdom/clan/craft rows appear.
--   4. Let the user correct parsing through commands instead of hidden patches.
--   5. Keep custom terms and custom palettes user-driven and persistent.
--
-- WHAT THIS PACKAGE DOES NOT DO
--   - It does not change DSL output text.
--   - It does not send game commands automatically.
--   - It does not infer religion/deity allegiance.
--   - It does not hardcode player names as logic.
--   - It does not special-case disputed names/titles outside normal commands.
--
-- PACKAGE SHAPE
--   One core script:
--     DslColors_Core_v1_0
--   One active trigger:
--     DslColors v1.0 line processor
--   One runtime alias:
--     dslcolor ...
--
-- SAVE FILE
--   DslColors uses one generic save file:
--     DSL_PeopleColors_data.lua
--   This file stores learned people, organizations, relations, teams, saved
--   titles, ignored terms, manual overrides, custom terms, and custom palettes.
--
-- IMPORTANT FLOWS
--   Titles:
--     Titles are exact leading phrases stripped before name capture.
--     Example: "Dread Pirate Valosiz Sha'falas" strips "Dread Pirate" only
--     if that exact phrase is a known title. It does not create "Dread" or
--     "Pirate" as separate titles.
--
--   Custom terms:
--     Custom terms are visual-only phrase coloring. They do not learn people,
--     organizations, titles, or relationships.
--
--   Custom palettes:
--     Custom palettes are saved color definitions. They do not color anything
--     by themselves until assigned through dslcolor term or name override.
--
--   Relationships:
--     Friend/enemy/war/peace are overlays. They should not replace factual
--     foreground identity colors.
--
-- PRIMARY COMMAND
--   dslcolor help
--
-- RELEASE NOTE
--   v1.0 keeps the stable cleanup base with release naming,
--   clearer help text, softer help/list colors, and verbose documentation.
--   The runtime logic, parsers, palette data, aliases, title flow, save/load,
--   custom terms, and custom palettes are preserved.
-- ============================================================

